The two \eqref{...} directives include a percent character ("PL" in this case) after the label key. This indicates to anyone doing autoref that the label key is a label. The percent character enables a coloRized numbering of the label segments.

The \label{...} directives include a page prefix ("S" in this case) to the label visibility. Only when maximized should the label display.


