Problem: A teacher asked her class a tricky question "When was the last time you cried?" A lively 3 year old Tim raised his hand "At when McDonald's birthday party yesterday". But the teacher insisted on finding one instance when you had cried since your last birthday. "It was when we came here yesterday." answered Tim. The question confused the teacher so she chose a different answer until one sleepy faced boy with glasses slowly made eyes   open and replied "At my last birthday party on June 1982, when Mom let me stay up one more night." Then the teacher realised that the boy knew that when his age, he would stayed up one more night'. "Is that the time you cried?" she asked. "Yes That was the time I cried." The boy said happily." Please tell me the time you cried last time," said  the teacher."Yeah. It was at my birthday party last year on May 13th," told the boy." And what happened that day?" the teacher asked. "When I opened my present, it was dead mac." "Oh, how sad! What did you do then?" the teacher asked. "I put the present under my birthday tree and got another present. When I opened the second present, it was alive. Then I cried." Three months later   ,Tim's mom found that McDonald's cat was dead and she was crying when she found the cat on the floor. So McDonald could not remember why he should have cried. "I cried because my mom gave McDonald to  me for my birthday. Then McDonald cried because he was afraid of being  alone." Answers why they were told.

